    "background_story": "Dexter was a botanist with a passion for rare and unusual plants. He spent most of his career studying the unique properties of Sagina, a small, delicate flowering plant found in the Arctic tundra. Dexter's fascination with Sagina led him to embark on numerous expeditions to the remote regions where it grew. His research revealed the plant's remarkable ability to thrive in harsh, nutrient-poor environments. As he delved deeper into his research, Dexter became increasingly obsessed with unlocking the secrets of Sagina's resilience. His colleagues began to call him the 'Sagina Whisperer' due to his extraordinary knowledge of the plant. Dexter's work eventually led to breakthroughs in the development of new, sustainable crops that could flourish in challenging conditions, earning him international recognition and accolades.",
